Third-party notices

lib/jpeg-encoder.cjs is vendored, not original to this project. It is the
Adobe/bytestrom JPEG encoder ported to JavaScript, under the 3-clause BSD
license reproduced in full at the top of that file. It is the only vendored
runtime file here.

Pixelblaze's pattern compiler and its LZString source-packer are Ben Hencke's
code, and this project does not contain or redistribute either one. They are
fetched at runtime from the web UI of whichever Pixelblaze you point pbz at
(GET /index.html.gz) and executed headless in node:vm — which is exactly why
the bytecode always matches your installed firmware. The same applies to the
pixel-map normalization used by `map set`. The captured web UI that the
hermetic tests run against is deliberately not committed; `npm run fixture`
pulls a copy from your own device into a gitignored path.

pbz is unofficial and not affiliated with or endorsed by ElectroMage.
Pixelblaze is Ben Hencke's product; this is a third-party tool for it.
